From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anton Palgunov <toxblh@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 01:36:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 94/99] v8: e2k: wasm SIMD widening by qppermb: extend, extmul,
 extending loads

extend_low/high, extmul_low/high and the loads with extension or zero
extension were LSX chains (an interleave with zero, shifts, even-lane
multiplies, a splat of the loaded value).  They are now not-LoongArch
instructions of the layer:

- vext/vextr: one qppermb by a constant index (zero bytes from a zero
  vector), then one arithmetic shift for 8 and 16 bits signed, the signs
  of the lanes as the other source for 32;
- vextmul: 8 bits both widened then qpmullh; 16 bits qpmullh and
  qpmulhh/qpmulhuh interleaved by one qppermb; 32 bits smulx/umulx;
- vzext: load64_zero/load32_zero are the load and one qppackdl.
---
